Subject: [PATCH 55/90] Faster starts with big mod packs: blockstates, mods'
 content and item definitions read by several threads

Binding the block models read each block's blockstate file in turn (the definitions of 880k states for 184 mods: 107 s); they are read up front by par_map. content_root read every mod's package and walked its folder one mod at a time (60 s for 200k files): several threads now, accepted in the same order. Item definitions were read one namespace at a time (hundreds with mods): all at once. Startup trace steps content.java_content, content.read_mods, content.resource_root and core.bake_states.bind/resolve/bake show where the content and model time goes.

UMP, 184 mods, warm start on an SSD: ready 438 -> 280 s (block models 114 -> 26 s, item models 39 -> 15 s, content read before the core tables 86 -> 42 s).
